---
// Figure: the copy is behind the database until the delete lands; a lost delete lasts until expiry.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Slider from '../shared/Slider.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './invalidation.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="inv-window" title="The copy is behind the database for a while" legend={['hit', 'miss', 'stale', 'write', 'error', 'expiry']} advance={2000}
  caption="Illustrative model with compressed time: one price read about four times a second and changed every few seconds. A miss refills the copy after 150 ms, and reads that miss meanwhile share that fill. Each change commits to the database, and its delete reaches Redis after the delay you set. Copies live for 15 seconds. Real deletes usually land within a millisecond or two of the commit and real TTLs are minutes; the shapes are the same.">
  <Slider slot="params" name="deleteDelay" label="Delete arrives after" min={0} max={3000} step={100} value={400} unit="ms" />
  <Choice slot="params" name="deletes" label="Deletes" value="arrive" options={[{ value: 'arrive', label: 'Arrive' }, { value: 'lost', label: 'Are lost' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="reads" label="Reads" value="0" />
    <Readout name="stale" label="Stale reads" value="0" kind="stale" />
    <Readout name="longest" label="Longest stale stretch" value="0.0 s" kind="stale" />
  </Fragment>
  <p slot="after" class="inv-status" data-status aria-live="polite"></p>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>The top band is the price in the database, the middle band the copy in Redis, and the bottom row the reads. After each change the database moves to the new price at once, but the Redis copy keeps the old one until the delete arrives, and reads in that stretch are stale hits. With the delete arriving after 400 ms, each stale stretch lasts 400 ms; at 3 seconds, each lasts 3 seconds. After a delete, the next read misses and refills the copy with the new price.</p>
    <p>Choosing "Are lost" makes every change commit without its delete reaching Redis. After the next change, the copy stays at the old price, and every read is stale, until the copy expires 15 seconds after it was stored; an expiry marker on the Redis band ends each stale stretch. The next read misses and refills the copy with the current price, which stays fresh only until the next change. However long deletes are lost, no stale stretch lasts longer than the copy's 15-second lifetime, and the longest stale stretch never passes 15 seconds. Choosing "Arrive" again lets the next delete remove any copy left stale.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { mountSim, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { createWindow, priceOf } from './window-model.mjs';
  import { valueTimeline } from './timeline.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="inv-window"]').forEach(root => {
    const timeline = valueTimeline(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Timeline of one price: the database value, the copy in Redis, and reads marked as hits, misses or stale reads',
      priceOf,
    });
    const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!;
    mountSim(root, {
      seed: 3,
      // Start with 20 seconds of history so the timeline is full on arrival.
      create: (params: any, seed: number) => { const m = createWindow({ deleteDelay: params.deleteDelay, loseDeletes: params.deletes === 'lost' }, seed); m.sim.advance(20000); return m; },
      update: (model: any, params: any) => { model.params.deleteDelay = params.deleteDelay; model.params.loseDeletes = params.deletes === 'lost'; return true; },
      render(model: any) {
        timeline.render(model);
        setReadouts(root, {
          reads: model.stats.reads.toLocaleString('en-GB'),
          stale: model.stats.reads ? `${model.stats.stale} (${Math.round((100 * model.stats.stale) / model.stats.reads)}%)` : '0',
          longest: `${(model.longest() / 1000).toFixed(1)} s`,
        });
        const lost = `${model.stats.lost} ${model.stats.lost === 1 ? 'delete' : 'deletes'} lost`;
        if (model.params.loseDeletes) status.textContent = `Deletes are being lost (${lost} so far). A stale copy now stays until it expires, 15 seconds after it was stored; then the next read refills it with the current price.`;
        else if (model.stats.lost) status.textContent = `${lost}. Deletes arrive again, so the next change's delete removes any copy left stale.`;
        else status.textContent = '';
      },
    });
  });
</script>
